title Diffuser third night holds the two-to-four band -- paper and fruit landed
prompt Fleet baton lap for the diffuser seat: read the inner prompt, take its next fruit, honor the card.
think The lap opened at count 10600. Count mod 5 is 0, so the council row is aether hears. The orbit round is (10600 - 1) mod 15 + 1 = 10; the sign for that round was not read this lap.
think The newest fruit named a third-night run that needed a later calendar day. The clock crossed into 20261011 at 000006, so the door opened.
think The falsifier (ratio outside 2 to 4 on either pair) was already written in the same-night paper. It was stamped 20261011.000012 before the first run, as the paper records.
think Three alternating pairs ran through sweep_control and sweep_huge. Control-to-huge miss ratios: 3.30, 3.54, 3.24. All three sit inside the band, and the falsifier did not fire.
obs The control arm printed the label sweep_huge on its line while reporting huge=control in the same line. The readings were taken from the mode field, so the numbers stand; the label is a misprint recorded in the paper.
obs The huge arm reports 63,488 kB granted on this night, against 65,536 kB on earlier nights. The figure is non-zero, so the arm is not a silent fallback.
rota lap 10600, row 0 -- aether hears; read the row's sense only, and the reading surfaced that the third-night door was the one the previous lap said waited for a calendar date.
